  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 227 AM EDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nStrong surface ridging will set up across the Eastern Seaboard \ntowards the middle of this week. Aloft, an even stronger ridge that \ncould be at or near all-time records with respect to 500-mb height \nanomalies will be building over the eastern US. With this setup, \nthere is increasing confidence that jet stream dynamics will cause a \npronounced cut-off low to form off the mainstream flow of an upper-\nlevel near eastern Canada. Guidance continues to hint at this trough \ndropping southward underneath the potent ridge across the Eastern \nSeaboard and approach South Florida mid-week around the Wednesday \nnight to Thursday time frame. This low also appears to \"absorb\" \nthe previous TUTT low over the Caribbean as it eventually advects \nacross the Florida Peninsula.\n\nIt remains too early to tell what exact impacts could occur from \nthis low advecting across the area late in the week, but in general \nit will provide extra forcing for ascent that will be able to \nproduce widespread showers and thunderstorms under a deep moisture \npresence (PWATs over 2.0\"). As conditions evolve over the next few \ndays, details will become more clear and communicated. As of now, we \ncan expect numerous showers and thunderstorms each day with risks \nfor heavy rainfall resulting in flooding. High temperatures each day \nwill continue to be in the upper 80s to low 90s.",
